cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use puremacro in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "puremacro: a Pyodide-compatible empirical and structural macroeconomics toolbox"
abstract: >-
  Pure-Python (numpy / scipy / pandas / matplotlib) toolbox for empirical and
  structural macroeconomics: SVAR identification, local projections, staggered
  DiD, GARCH, growth-at-risk, heterogeneous-agent VFI and Bayesian DSGE models,
  and free narrative text-as-data uncertainty indices. Runs in the browser via
  Pyodide; no MATLAB, Stata, or paid data feeds required.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alonso Ortiz"
    given-names: "Jorge"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jalonso1979/puremacro"
keywords:
  - macroeconomics
  - econometrics
  - structural VAR
  - local projections
  - heterogeneous-agent models
  - uncertainty
  - Pyodide
